   const term=domain==="regulation"?p.regulator:domain==="trading"||domain==="structure"?p.venues:domain==="currency"?p.currency:p.terms[(di+si)%p.terms.length];
   const objective=title+" — "+market+".";
   const explanation=lessonAnswer(domain,market,term,si,title);
   const gains=["A clear mental model you can use in real research.","The ability to identify the local rule instead of importing one from another market.","The ability to trace cause → mechanism → consequence.","A decision question you can use before relying on this concept.","The ability to connect market mechanics to company economics.","A repeatable primary-source research method.","A defence against the misconception most likely to create a bad conclusion.","Evidence that you can apply the concept to a real market event.","Proof that you can use the concept, not merely recognise it.","Transferable mastery: explain and apply the concept in a new situation."];
   const examples=["Find one real "+market+" security or event where this concept is visible.","Open the current official rule or exchange explanation and identify the exact mechanism.","Trace one real example from investor action to market or company outcome.","Write the one investor question that must be answered before relying on this concept.","Show where this concept affects cash, ownership, financing, risk or valuation for one company.","Trace one important claim to its original filing, exchange notice, regulator rule or issuer document.","Write what evidence would prove the tempting assumption wrong.","Reconstruct the concept from a real company, filing, transaction or market event.","Solve a small scenario and separate assumptions from verified facts.","Explain the concept without looking, then transfer it to a different market or company."];
   const chinaOrientation=market==="China"&&domain==="orientation"?{
     action:["Open CSRC's A/B/H-share investor explanation and write one sentence defining each share class; then identify which exchange or listing venue each one belongs to.","Open the official SSE and SZSE English market pages. Write down the role of each exchange, then place STAR Market and ChiNext under the correct exchange.","Open the official Stock Connect eligibility pages. Pick one mainland-listed security and determine whether Northbound access is available and which investor category rules apply.","Choose a Chinese company with more than one listed share line. Record the company, ticker, exchange, share class and trading currency for each line before comparing prices.","Take the same company's mainland and Hong Kong lines and check whether they represent the same economic claim, whether the share lines are interchangeable, and what currency each price uses.","Use SSE, SZSE, HKEX and CSRC primary pages to build a source map for one Chinese security; save the exact page that supports each fact.","Find a Chinese security that a foreign investor cannot simply buy through your assumed route. Write down the exact eligibility condition that blocks or changes the route.","Reconstruct one real Chinese company from operating business to listed share line, exchange, board and Stock Connect status using primary pages only.","Create a one-page China market map using three real securities: one SSE, one SZSE and one Hong Kong-listed H-share. Cite the source beside every classification.","Without opening the sources, explain the five-part route: share class → venue/board → investor eligibility → trading/custody route → ownership and disclosure."],
     trap:["Treating A-shares, B-shares and H-shares as interchangeable tickers for the same investor.","Thinking Shanghai and Shenzhen are interchangeable labels and overlooking the board-specific rules inside each exchange.","Assuming Stock Connect gives a foreign investor access to every mainland-listed stock.","Comparing two tickers because the company name is identical without checking the share class and listing venue.","Assuming a lower Hong Kong or mainland price automatically means one line is cheaper when currency, liquidity and share-line mechanics differ.","Using a financial website's country summary as the authority for a current access or market-structure rule.","Assuming that a security visible on a data terminal is necessarily purchasable through your own investor route.","Starting with the company story and forgetting to identify the exact security being analysed.","Building a market map from memory and then treating the map as current without checking official sources.","Saying 'I know the China market' without being able to distinguish ownership of a company from ownership of a particular listed share line."],
     proof:["Explain the difference between an A-share, B-share and H-share and give one concrete implication of each for an investor.","Name the two mainland exchanges and state which exchange operates STAR Market and which operates ChiNext.","Explain why a foreign investor can see a mainland stock in a database but still not be able to buy it through a particular route.","Given two tickers for one Chinese company, list the four facts you would verify before comparing their prices.","Explain why two share lines of the same operating company can have different prices without one necessarily being economically cheaper.","Point to the primary source you would use for exchange structure, Stock Connect eligibility and regulatory education, and explain why each source fits its job.","Given a mainland ticker, explain the sequence of checks required before concluding that a foreign investor can purchase it.","Take a real Chinese company and verbally walk from the operating business to the exact listed security an investor owns.","Show your three-security market map and explain one access difference between the SSE/SZSE securities and the H-share.","Answer this: if someone says 'I want to buy a Chinese stock,' what five pieces of information must you ask for before you know what they mean?"]
   }:null;
   const actionText=chinaOrientation?.action[si]||("Study "+domain+" in "+market+" using "+term+". Check the current primary source and record what you found.");
   const trapText=chinaOrientation?.trap[si]||("Watch for importing a familiar "+domain+" assumption into "+market+" without checking the local mechanism.");
   const proofText=chinaOrientation?.proof[si]||("Prove your understanding of "+domain+" by explaining it in your own words, giving one "+market+" example, and naming the evidence that could change your answer.");
   const tests=["Can you explain it without repeating the definition?","Can you identify what is local and what transfers?","Can you predict the consequence if one input changes?","Can you state what evidence would change your conclusion?","Can you connect it to an actual company outcome?","Can another person reproduce your important fact from the source?","Can you identify the assumption most likely to fail?","Can you reconstruct the result from original evidence?","Can you solve the scenario with explicit assumptions?","Can you teach the concept and apply it somewhere new?"];
   return {id:slug(market)+"-"+(di*10+si+1),number:di*10+si+1,domain,title,stage:phase,objective,explanation,whyItMatters:why,action:actionText,trap:trapText,answer:explanation,verification:"Verify current, time-sensitive details against the relevant official source before using them in a real decision. PirePoint provides general education, not individualized legal, tax or investment advice.",learn:"Learn the mechanism, then explain it in your own words.",difficulty:si<3?"beginner":si<7?"intermediate":"advanced",proof:proofText,benefit:gains[si],example:market+" application: use "+term+" as the anchor for one real security, filing, transaction or market event involving "+domain+".",test:proofText,master:si===9?"Transfer the idea to a new market, company or transaction and explain what changes.":"Complete the test and keep the evidence you used.",primarySources:p.sources||[]};
